Database migrations (Alembic).

Alembic owns the enterprise schema. `alembic upgrade head` runs automatically
from the container entrypoint, and `DB_AUTO_CREATE=false` in the image stops the
application from also calling `create_all`, so the two cannot disagree.

Local development still defaults to `create_all` (DB_AUTO_CREATE unset), which
builds a throwaway SQLite database from the models.

Common commands:

    alembic upgrade head                      # apply everything
    alembic downgrade -1                      # roll back one revision
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..."  # after changing models.py
    alembic current                           # show the applied revision

The URL comes from DATABASE_URL via normalize_database_url(), so a synchronous
driver string is upgraded to its async equivalent automatically.
